Title: yawn reports project directives that contradict or shadow the harness
Created: 2026-10-27
Author: Minh Ha-Duong

--- log ---
2026-10-27T05:45Z Minh Ha-Duong created

--- body ---
## Context
Parent: 1229. `yawn` is project-oriented and currently has no check comparing
a project's own directives against the harness.

Scope: project `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/rules/`,
`.claude/skills/`, `.agents/skills/` against the loaded harness rules and
skills. Never the harness against itself (that is 1233). In the harness repo
itself the check is a `skip`.

Findings, three kinds, each with a *why*:
- contradiction: a local instruction that inverts a harness instruction;
- shadowing: a local skill or rule with a harness name (mechanical), or one
  taking a harness skill's responsibility (judged);
- repeated procedure: a local copy of a harness procedure.

A local override that states its reason in place is `ok (reasoned)`; a
silent override or a copy is `warn`. Example of reasoned: arena's
`CLAUDE.md` replaces merge-by-PR with `git merge --no-ff` because the repo
has no forge.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Name-collision shadowing is a script under `scripts/`, called from the
      yawn body, with a test that fires on a fixture project shadowing a
      harness skill name (positive control) and stays quiet on one that does not
- [ ] Judged findings read skill descriptions first and full bodies only where
      descriptions overlap
- [ ] Each finding names the local file, the harness file, and the
      governing instruction; output fits the existing yawn report format
- [ ] Degrades to `skip` with a reason when the project has no local directives
- [ ] `yawn` stays a reporter: no fixes, no tickets

## Imagine (raid 2026-10-27)

**Premise holds.** `skills/yawn/SKILL.md:33-104` (checks 1-13) has no local-versus-harness comparison; the only pass is the prompt at `scripts/prompt-project-coherence.sh:40`, called from `scripts/on-start-context.sh:36-38`, whose lines 17-31 enumerate exactly this ticket's local sources.

**Simplest path.** (1) `scripts/project_shadow.py <project>`: local skill and rule names against harness `skills/*` and `rules/*`, reusing `skill_frontmatter.load` (`scripts/skill_frontmatter.py:44`); JSON, one line per collision (local file, harness file, governing instruction). (2) Move the harness-self and linked-worktree guard (`prompt-project-coherence.sh:9-14`) into the script so the harness yields `skip`; 1232 deletes the prompt script and would otherwise lose it. (3) Yawn check 14: run the script, then the judged pass (descriptions first, bodies only on overlap); one table row plus bullets, placed before Output format. (4) `tests/test_project_shadow.py` with tmp fixture projects (positive: shadows a harness skill name; negative: does not).

**Antipatterns.** YAGNI: no Python prose parsing for contradictions; the judged part stays with the model. Duplication: share the source enumeration or note two small lists.

**Criterion proposals.** (a) The script emits the `skip` reason; test the harness-self and the no-directives skips. (b) `ok (reasoned)` made operational: the reason sits in the same file within a few lines of the override; arena `CLAUDE.md` "no remote" is the live fixture. (c) Output is stable for 1231, which routes it.

**Blind-spot pass (raid 2026-10-27), folded in.** (1) Scope includes the project's own top-level `skills/*` when they are projected into the user skill namespace (arena's `skills/arena`, linked from `~/.claude/skills/arena`), not only `.claude/skills/` and `.agents/skills/`. (2) Project skill roots are per runtime (Vibe `.vibe/skills`, `adapters/pilot-support.json:55`; Pi, Codex): take the folder list from the adapter declarations, not a hardcoded list, and judge shadowing against each runtime's precedence. (3) yawn is the cross-runtime proof slice (`adapters/README.md:142-152`): the check calls its script through the runtime-supplied `IDH_ROOT` seam and `tests/test_skill_seam.py` passes. (4) The finding record is the 1231 contract: kind, local file, harness file, governing instruction, verdict (`ok (reasoned)` / `warn`), proposed disposition and destination (project or harness); `tests/test_yawn_molt_suggestion.py` pins the shared yawn/molt text. Raid assumption, author may overrule: the judged half also runs when molt calls yawn from lair, since it is scoped to one project with local directives.
